Description: aic8800_fdrv (USB): log the firmware patch table and overheard 4-address frames at debug level
 Two error-level dumps fill the kernel's log on a working system:
 .
  - every word of the firmware patch table as it is written ("patch_tbl: ..."), on every firmware
    load: 555 lines on an AIC8800DC, each time the device is reset;
  - every 4-address frame received while the driver is built without CONFIG_SUPPORT_4ADDR, with a hex
    dump of the frame, before it is dropped. A mesh WiFi network's access points send these between
    themselves, so a station near one logs several a second.
 .
 On a board with a small kernel log buffer (16 KB), the two overwrite everything else within a
 minute or two, other drivers' errors with them. Both are now dev_dbg/print_hex_dump_debug (dynamic
 debug can turn them on again); the frames are still dropped as before.
Author: NomDeTom
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-10
---
Index: aic8800/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_compat_8800dc.c
===================================================================
--- aic8800.orig/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_compat_8800dc.c
+++ aic8800/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_compat_8800dc.c
@@ -2749,7 +2749,7 @@
 
     if (!err && (i < size)) {
         for (i =(128/4); i < (size/4); i +=2) {
-            AICWFDBG(LOGERROR, "patch_tbl:  %x  %x\n", dst[i], dst[i+1]);
+            AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, "patch_tbl:  %x  %x\n", dst[i], dst[i+1]);
             err = rwnx_send_dbg_mem_write_req(rwnx_hw, dst[i], dst[i+1]);
         }
         if (err) {
